The do...while loop is similar to the while loop, but the instructions in the code block
are executed before the condition is checked. Use this form when you must have the
code executed at least once, even if the expression is false:
do
{
blink(); // call a function to turn an LED on and off
}
while (analogRead(sensorPin) > 100);

